# vehje-runtime-driver. compiler-side runtime dispatch

The compiler-side embedding and dispatch over the wire C ABI: serialize a
`Checked` residual, hand it to the embedded Zig runtime, and map results and
diagnostics back. It also holds the safe, bounds-checked reader over the
value-arena a produced value crosses back in, and the validation pass a value
passes before the host reads it. The one framework crate with a `std` role, for
the dlopen of the runtime artifact. Compile-time dispatch, no `dyn`, no plugin
shared-object loading at the compiler layer. `#![no_std]` on the core paths.
